# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Argonaut — files that must NEVER reach GitHub
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── SECRETS (bot token, admin key) ──────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
server/.env

# Safety net: stray notes at the repo ROOT are where secrets get
# pasted by accident. These patterns are deliberately anchored with
# a leading "/" so they only apply to the root folder — an unanchored
# *token* would also swallow legitimate files like server/set-token.bat.
/*.txt
/*token*
/*secret*

# ── MOVED OUT (this repo is PUBLIC and GitHub Pages serves every
#    file in it verbatim — see the note in README). The training
#    pipeline and the bot backend now live in the sibling folder
#    "Argonaut-Private/" so they are never published again.
ml/
server/

# ── DEPENDENCIES (thousands of files, reinstalled with npm i)
node_modules/
server/node_modules/

# ── USER DATA (real people's scans + feedback labels) ───────
data/
server/data/

# ── Python build artefacts ──────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ── Scratch / local-only ────────────────────────────────────
_vidtmp/
*.log
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── OS + editor noise (OneDrive folder, so expect these) ────
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.tmp
~$*
